notes.notes:
This is a major update, which saw many aspects of the game reviewed and polished a bit.

Most notably, of course, 25 different arenas were added to the game.
They get unlocked as you progress, and offer variety to matches; some requiring quite different strategies. Old good plain empty field is still occasionally added to the mix.

Other changes include:

Quality of Life

 Hints for starters that will help new players make their first step;
 Match starting animation is now skippable! Just click or press any key;
 Game performance was optimised. Not that the game really required it, but it will help battery charge last longer when played on a laptop;


Visuals

 Gem brightness was tuned;
 Conquered blocks of gems now fuse together into bigger gems!
 Fixed a visual glitch where next move selection animation continued to play while in Esc menu;


Audio

 Some minor tuning, balance is better, erm, balanced;
 A different sound effect when turn results in a large area surrounded and taken over;


Achievements

 New achievement: Explorer;
 Achievement conditions reworded to be applicable to variable field size: Resounding Victory and So Close;
 Some achievements will now indicate progress toward them;


Thank you for reading this!

Please share in Discussions section which changes you liked or not quite, and report any bugs you notice.

Following on players' feedback and reviews, the game has been updated.

Changes in 1.0.1:

 Added music and SFX volume settings on the Esc menu;
 Added Quit button on Victory/Defeat screen;
 Added window/taskbar icons (might still be missing with some DPI settings).


Thank you for your feedback and support!
